- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-12$ | {{field-3}} | {{field-4}} |  |  |" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $M$ by $\\frac{2}{3}$ and each entry of $N$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{3}M+2N & =\\frac{2}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}6 & 0 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 6 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & \\frac{1}{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 15 \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot (-12) & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot (-1) & 2\\cdot 0 \\\\ 2\\cdot (-2) & 2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2} & 2\\cdot (-1)\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 10 \\\\ -8 & 4 & 0\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}6 & -2 & 0 \\\\ -4 & 1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4+6 & 0-2 & 10+0 \\\\ -8-4 & 4+1 & 0-2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}10 & -2 & 10 \\\\ -12 & 5 & -2\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186392959 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "a6727fdd-a614-5ead-9273-08c0a7fec997" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Linear Combination of Two Matrices"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "43f31230-0191-5a33-9bb6-0fa7b614f351" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 15 & 6 \\\\ 2 & 14 & 11\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392961} {:answer/id #uuid "dbcc9309-5767-5a6f-9aa6-d329adc4d01c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392962} {:answer/id #uuid "4cf8254f-ba83-5a63-900a-3e1c1e498e5e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 14 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 15\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392963} {:answer/id #uuid "8d6b4403-a5b1-58bb-a750-3f579f43ba12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 10\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392964} {:answer/id #uuid "fb62ffb5-df7e-583b-a72f-d8637500006d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -2 & 11 & 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392965}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dbcc9309-5767-5a6f-9aa6-d329adc4d01c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 14\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392962} :answer-field/id #uuid "18f4324f-d0d0-557c-90a1-7c9edabe233c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392960}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "6a24360c-add3-5cc0-aec3-f47a46ccf0fe" :question/math-academy-id "q-69642" :question/problem "Calculate $\\frac{1}{3}G+2H$, where\n$G=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}$\nand\n$H=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix}.$" :question/worked-solution "We multiply each entry of $G$ by $\\frac{1}{3}$ and each entry of $H$ by $2,$ and then add the resulting matrices, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}G+2H & =\\frac{1}{3}\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ -12 & 9 & 6\\end{bmatrix}+2\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ 3 & 4 & 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 3 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 15 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-12) & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 9 & \\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 6\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2\\cdot 1 & 2\\cdot 2 & 2\\cdot 5 \\\\ 2\\cdot 3 & 2\\cdot 4 & 2\\cdot 6\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 5 \\\\ -4 & 3 & 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & 10 \\\\ 6 & 8 & 12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1+2 & 2+4 & 5+10 \\\\ -4+6 & 3+8 & 2+12\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 6 & 15 \\\\ 2 & 11 & 14\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Calculating a Linear Combination of Two Matrices"}]}
